# DURABLE REPRO for the composite-print raw-address defect (TODO.md HIGH,
# "print(<non-Displayable composite>) prints a RAW ADDRESS", filed
# 2026-07-25, widened 2026-07-31 by Round XX pass 6, "durable repro still
# owed since 2026-07-25 filing"). Committed by R37 (2026-08-08) after the
# R37 executor rediscovered the defect during Phase 2 sweep debugging
# (originally misdiagnosed as a Vector move-and-return issue — the real
# root is `print(<Vector>)` prints a raw address regardless of how the
# Vector was produced; move-and-return is not involved).
#
# Class: Core #4 sibling drift (`E_NonPrintableInterpolation` fires on the
# f-string path — `docs/language-reference.md:2904` — but is NOT wired on
# the `print(arg)` path) + Core #10 (lowering arm accepts syntax it cannot
# render).
#
# Family: Struct / Enum / Vector / Tuple / Set (+ Dict on `gg`) — a NEG
# fixture per costume owed at fix time; this minimal repro pins the
# Vector[int] costume, which is the most commonly reachable (any user who
# `print(<vector>)` s a Vector hits this).
#
# Wired at `tests/integration.rs::print_composite_raw_address` (`#[ignore]`d
# — asserts the CORRECT / intended output: the Vector CONTENTS
# (formatted as `[10, 20, 30]` or the compiler's canonical
# vector-display), NOT a raw address `281474...`). Un-ignore + promote out
# of `known_gaps/` when either (a) `print(<non-Displayable composite>)` is
# rejected at check (matching the f-string path), OR (b) the compiler
# gains a canonical composite-display for the base composites (matching
# ggdef's `[1, 2, 3]` rendering).
#
# RED-verified at HEAD (2026-08-08, HEAD 900bd06f7 + R37 chain): building
# and running THIS fixture prints e.g. `281474799179512` — a raw pointer
# where `[10, 20, 30]` (or the language's chosen canonical) is intended.

int main():
    Vector[int] items = [10, 20, 30]
    # BUG: prints e.g. `281474799179512` (raw heap address of the Vector's
    # underlying buffer). ggdef prints `[10, 20, 30]`. See TODO.md HIGH.
    print(items)
    return 0
